t then on the  third tier i broke in half this organic  raspberry mini bar that i got from  my local grocery store called h-e-b and  these are super healthy  and really good for you because they  have quinoa and chia seeds and then  finally on the top tier i put a babybel  light  cheese oh my god i am lowkey obsessed  with this snack tower  i would totally buy this for my toddler  and then secretly steal it for myself if  i don't know we ever conquer covet and i  get to leave the house one day with a  snack tower  in tow  anyways we definitely have some fun  snacks here i see some carbs in the  pretzels and the cereal bar and the  chocolate  we got a little bit of fat in the  almonds and a little bit of protein in  the baby bell now again a quick note on  yogurt pretzels these are legit one of  my  favorite sweet and salty snacks of all  time  and the trader joe ones are so good but  again i want to flag the health halo  status  just because they have the word yogurt  in the title doesn't mean  they're actually made with real yogurt  in fact the first ingredient in this  product is cane sugar  not actual yogurt and a serving of six  twists  have 18 grams of added sugar again  totally fine in moderation and one of my  personal favorite snacks  but often these health halos give people  the drive to eat snacks like this  in excess while swearing off something  that they maybe like  more like chocolate coated pretzels and  they see that as the bad  option and that often is how scarcity  mentality  starts substituting a food that you love  for food that you  think that you should eat i'm not saying  that this is what's happening with  caroline  she may just totally love them like i do  but i am flagging this as like an fyi  for you folks who are watching at home  now i do notice that we're having a  snack but not an actual  meal here and skipping meals in favor of  just having snacks  is actually a pretty typical pattern for  a lot of teens  but not fueling your body with regular  satiating meals  can often cause sugar cravings later on  in the day  since we're looking for those quick hits  of energy all day long  so for caroline i would really suggest  building this into a bigger more  substantial meal  with a little bit more protein and  healthy fat on board  so if she wanted it to be handheld and  convenient like the snack tower we could  throw some roasted chickpeas or some dry  roasted nuts into the snack tower  and then maybe pair it with like a wrap  or sandwich with some nutritious veggies  and a really nutritious spread like  hummus in there  let's take a look at what's next my  post-workout snacks are  probably my favorite because that is  when i'm so hungry  and all i want to do is just eat some  fruit then i went ahead and picked out  an  apple that i liked opened up my fridge  and looked for the fruit that i was  craving for the day  and that happened to be raspberries and  strawberries which are my  favorites okay so normally fruit is a  great nutrient-dense snack choice if  you're feeling like something light  especially if we're going with like a  higher fiber fruit option  like an apple or berries but because  caroline specifically  just finished a workout and she didn't  really have  a full meal before working out i would  definitely want to  beef this up with a source of protein so  she could throw those berries into a  protein shake or serve them on top of  some greek yogurt or cottage cheese  or she could pair the apple with like a  couple of hard-boiled eggs  so again it's not about taking food away  it's really just about adding something  to help boost up the satiety factor and  the nutrition  let's move along to dinner and today we  are having spaghetti  and salad with strawberries and apples  butter lettuce  pecans apples strawberries and then  cheese i made this try usually  i drink my chai cold but i bought these  packets from heb  so this looks like an awesome balanced  dinner and  totally something that i would make at  home so we've got protein and fat in the  beef  pecans and cheese lots of fiber rich  carbs  from the pasta and fruit and then a nice  variety of colorful antioxidant rich  produce as well  it's a simple accessible classic family  meal that  i'm sure definitely hits the spot and  also a recipe that would be really great  cooking inspiration for a lot of her  teen  young viewers all right lovelies we have  made it through  dinner let's talk about the stats and a  trigger warning  i am going to be talking numbers so of  course feel free to like skip  this piece if it's triggering to you so  my best  estimation is that caroline is consuming  around 2  000 calories with about 54 of calories  from carbs  34 from fat and 14 from protein  so all of that is within the american  pediatrics association recommendations  for really growing active teens so  nothing  majorly concerning right there she is a  little bit low in some key nutrients  most notably iron and vitamin d for a  growing teen  and as she already alluded to herself  her diet does contain  more added sugar than what she herself  says that she would like  so most health authorities recommend no  more than 6 teaspoons  or 25 grams of added sugar per day  now in this day at least caroline was  getting around 5 times that amount  now if i'm being honest when i was a  teen i totally did the same so  i am hesitant to even bring it up  because i don't want  any teen watching to go cutting out  carbs  teens are growing like they're active  and they actually need a lot of carbs to  thrive so  i mentioned this not i repeat  not to suggest that caroline cut back on  carbs  i love bread but there's a difference  nutritionally between  the types of foods that contain a lot of  added or  free sugars and foods that contain whole  naturally occurring sugars so whole food  sources of carbs  have their sugars bound up with healthy  fats fiber  protein and micronutrients so this is  really where we want to focus